Z||000000||Nyte||01-15-2001||05:55 PM||||What engines can I use to rebuild for my '84 SE without rewiring everything from the dash back?  What cars use the Iron Duke or some similar engine that's compatible?<P>Or is it really <I>all that hard</I> to put a six cylinder in an '84?  If I could, what should i use?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/devilteeth.gif">      <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>      <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/devilsmile.gif">      <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of 95-99 Chevy S-10)</B><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/fender4profile.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/pontiaclogo.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||theogre||01-15-2001||07:48 PM||||The distributor version was used thru 1986 in a number of GM cars. Check Cutlas Calais/Ciera and grand am. You'll have to change all the pulleys and brackets but the rest is the same. It changes to the DIS motor for 87 models.<P>any decent scrap yard has an interchange book that tells you what years and cars that block was used in.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||01-15-2001||07:52 PM||||How 'bout the GM 3.0 liter industrial engine. They use em in Toyota  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and Hyster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> forklifts. I'm not sure if it would bolt up, but if it does it would be an easy way to get some cubes under the hood. They use the same ignition system as a Fiero, and the TBI could be adapted fairly easily. In a Toyota with a LP fuel system and 2500 RPM governed speed, it makes 90 hp. OK, it might not be an easy swap, but it sure would be unique!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000003||KRMFiero||01-15-2001||10:23 PM||||I have a GM 3.0 Marine engine, we took it out of out boar and put a 5.7 in....   That 3.0 pushed our boar at 25 mph all day at 4,000 rpm (28 foot bayliner with a comand bridge)... but the bolt pattern is like the same as a Chevy SB... would not bolt right up but it would be a awsome racing engine (can hangle constant high speeds)<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<P>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nyte||01-16-2001||05:21 PM||||OK, how about this...<P>What cars used the same Iron Duke that's in my 84' SE?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/devilteeth.gif">      <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>      <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/devilsmile.gif">      <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of 95-99 Chevy S-10)</B><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/fender4profile.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/pontiaclogo.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||overlord||01-16-2001||09:20 PM||||the replacement duck i put in my fiero came out of a pontiac 6000. It is the same engine. I didnt put it in myslef but there  were some slight differences so i was told...but all in all its the exact same thing..........wish i knew  how many miles were on it.||||reg||1
